DO-WHILE loop

class GFG {
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        // Declaring and initialization expression
        int c = 1;

        // Do-while loop
        do {
            // Body of do-while loop
            // Print statement
            System.out.println("Hello World");

            // Update expression
            c++;
        }
        // Test expression
        while (c < 6);
    }
}

OUTPUT :- Hello World
          Hello World
          Hello World
          Hello World
          Hello World

Difference between break and continue:
              Break                                                                 Continue

Terminates the loop immediately.                               Skips the current iteration and continues with the next one

Transfers control outside the loop.                               Transfers control to the next loop iteration.

Can be used with loops and switch statements.                     Can be used only inside loops.

Stops further execution of the loop body completely.              Skips only the remaining statements in the current iteration.

Can be used with labeled loops.                                   Can also be used with labeled loops.


